                <pb facs="0912" n="776" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg776"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3351: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moore</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-25T19:00:00-05:00">April 25, 1929—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>47. Before answering your 81, April 24, 10 p.m., the Department would like to
                    know results of the interview between President Leguia and the Chilean
                    Ambassador regarding the scope of the suggestion of settlement to be made by the
                    President which your 80, April 24, 2 p.m., promised.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
